  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires all incidents reported within 24h, including under investigation, and customer notice within 72h. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% threshold but no automatic sales stop, while requiring numeric per-model failure rates to customers; S3 mandates remote shut-off on new units immediately and retrofit within six years with an alternative. S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months, and S5 mandates recall above 8 incidents/100k with 10-day customer notice but lacks a serious-injury clause."
